> Outstanding natural conditions, a[ mountain] sports offering that is unequalled and an excellent tourist infrastructure, together with cordial hospitality, outstanding cuisine and an inspiring combination of tradition and modernity - these are the ingredients that make Lech Zürs am Arlberg one of the leading holiday resorts in the[ Alpine] region. "More time, more space" in a[ breathtaking]ly[ diverse] landscape.
The Flexenbahn cableway will open in the winter of 2016/17 and will make[ skiing] at the Arlberg even more varied and comfortable. With the help of the new link between Zürs and Stuben/Rauz, skiers can easily reach all resorts at the Arlberg on skis. That will make the Arlberg[ skiing] area the largest contiguous[ skiing] area in Austria! With 87[ ski] lifts, 305 kilometres of[ ski] runs and 200 kilometres of high[ Alpine] deep powder snow runs available,[ virtually] unlimited[ skiing] and snowboarding enjoyment is guaranteed. Whether beginner, advanced or simply in search of adventure[:] Deep powder snow[ slopes], blue, red and black runs and nursery[ slopes] offer optimal conditions for every level and taste. The Ski-Arlberg card is particularly advantageous as it enables "all inclusive" use of all lifts and cable cars of Lech Zürs and the neighbouring towns of Warth-Schröcken, Stuben, St. Christoph and St.[ Anton] from 2 December 2016 to 23 April 2017.
The mountain world of Lech Zürs is a power place, ideal for building up your energy. It is calmer in the summer than in the winter, so summer is the perfect time to surround yourself with nature and concentrate on your mind, body and spirit. It does not matter how slow or fast you go. Whether you prefer strolling, hiking or jogging, and whether you stay on the magnificent Lech Zürs plateaus or go uphill, you will be able to focus your thoughts when moving at your own pace. Exercising in the fresh air will not only help to train your body, but will also promote mental and spiritual regeneration. It is at least as good for rest and recreation as it is for fitness. Summer season[:] 23 June to 2 oct[ober] 2017.

